.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt ERR_LOAD_STRINGS 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ERR_load_strings ,
.Nm ERR_PACK ,
.Nm ERR_get_next_error_library
.Nd load arbitrary error strings
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/err.h
.Ft int
.Fo ERR_load_strings
.Fa "int lib"
.Fa "ERR_STRING_DATA *str"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo ERR_get_next_error_library
.Fa void
.Fc
.Ft unsigned long
.Fo ERR_PACK
.Fa "int lib"
.Fa "int func"
.Fa "int reason"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn ERR_load_strings
registers error strings for library number
.Fa lib .
.Pp
.Fa str
is an array of error string data:
.Bd -literal
 typedef struct ERR_string_data_st
 {
     unsigned long error;
     char *string;
 } ERR_STRING_DATA;
.Ed
.Pp
The error code is generated from the library number and a function and
reason code:
.Sy error
=
.Pf ERR_PACK( Fa lib ,
.Fa func ,
.Fa reason Ns ).
.Fn ERR_PACK
is a macro.
.Pp
The last entry in the array is {0,0}.
.Pp
.Fn ERR_get_next_error_library
can be used to assign library numbers to user libraries at run time.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn ERR_load_strings
returns 1 for success and 0 for failure.
.Fn ERR_PACK
returns the error code.
.Fn ERR_get_next_error_library
returns zero on failure, otherwise a new library number.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ERR_load_strings 3
